    "title": "Soup sold at H-E-B recalled after a customer reported it didn't match the label - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Peter Warren ,\n5 hours ago H-E-B Bridgeland at Village Green at Bridgeland Central opened Oct. 30, 2024. (Marissa Luck/Houston Chronicle) A soup sold at H-E-B has been recalled after a customer reported the soup on the label wasn't the product they received.\nMeal Simple brand soup labeled as Red Lentil Dal Soup in 16-ounce containers, which have been on sale since November with a \"best by\" date of Jan. 11, 2026, are being recalled.\nMOST EXCITING: Houston’s most over-the-top Christmas bars and restaurants\nThe mistake led a risk of customers consuming undeclared milk, which could cause an allergic reaction for some people.\n\"The recall was initiated after a consumer notified the firm that the product in the container labeled as Meal Simple Red Lentil Dal Soup was a poultry and rice soup,\" the recall notice reads.\n\"After an internal investigation it was discovered that Meal Simple Turkey & Wild Rice Soup contains milk as an ingredient. The Meal Simple Red Lentil Dal Soup does not include milk as an ingredient, nor does it declare milk on the label. The root cause investigation is ongoing.\"\nPeople can return the soup for a full refund.\nSign up for Houston Chronicle newsletters here\nRead the original article on houstonchronicle.com\n4",
